From c013a1d7d4b593b9dfbeee979bb93493575810bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:35:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 255/259] CED skip: keep one decoder row of unread nonfinal
 chunks, stop on shortened successors

An eligible prefill chunk that is truncated anyway, ends on the scheduler's
aligned chunk boundary and is followed by at least the replay reach of prefill
rows keeps only its last decoder row, whose logits the runner discards; no
later decoder or draft window reaches back into it. nonfinal_limits computes
the per-request kept-row limits the TileLang requests kernel takes, and
plan_ced keeps the window bound as the decoder's maximum query length.

Startup requires TileLang, aligned chunked prefill, DSpark and a chunk
threshold covering the target and draft replay reach (199 rows at k=5), and
raises otherwise. Multimodal requests are ineligible. A skipped chunk records
its promised successor, and a changed or shortened successor raises before any
metadata or GPU work: no replay floor, environment switch or fallback.
